    "text": "To determine the total number of bird eggs June found, we need to add up the eggs from all the nests she discovered. Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **First Tree Nest:**\n   - There are 2 nests in the first tree.\n   - Each nest has 5 eggs.\n   - Total eggs in the first tree: \\(2 \\times 5 = 10\\)\n\n2. **Second Tree Nest:**\n   - There is 1 nest in the second tree.\n   - This nest has 3 eggs.\n   - Total eggs in the second tree: \\(1 \\times 3 = 3\\)\n\n3. **Front Yard Nest:**\n   - There is 1 nest in the front yard.\n   - This nest has 4 eggs.\n   - Total eggs in the front yard: \\(1 \\times 4 = 4\\)\n\nNow, we add up all the eggs from the three nests:\n\\[\n10 \\text{ (first tree)} + 3 \\text{ (second tree)} + 4 \\text{ (front yard)} = 17\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of bird eggs June found is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).",
